  "headline": "Heat Advisory issued November 3 at 2:56AM AST until November 3 at 2:00PM AST by NWS San Juan PR",
  "description": "* WHAT...This level of heat affects most individuals sensitive to\nheat, especially those without effective cooling and/or adequate\nhydration.\n\n* WHERE...Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands.\n\n* WHEN...From 9 AM this morning to 2 PM AST this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...High temperatures or elevated heat indices can worsen\nsymptoms in people with chronic conditions. They can also increase\nthe risk of heat-related illness among individuals sensitive to\nheat with inadequate cooling or hydration. These risks are highest\nacross coastal areas, lowlands, interior valleys, and urban zones.",
  "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids, stay in an air-conditioned room, stay out of\nthe sun, and check up on relatives and neighbors.",
